# {{PROJECT_NAME}} - Prologue
# The engine loads this file first when the player starts a new game.
# Execution begins at @label start. From here, [goto] routes to other scenario files.
# Replace the placeholder content below with your actual opening scene.

@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_prologue
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}

# ─── Entry Point ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This label is the game's first frame. Everything the player sees at launch starts here.
# The @scenario ID above ("{{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_prologue") is how other files reference this
# file in [goto] commands — e.g. [goto {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_prologue:start].

@label start
[show lavender center {{LAVENDER_EXPR}}]
narrator: Welcome to {b}{{PROJECT_NAME}}{/b}.
narrator: This prologue script is the entry point of the game. It routes to other .vns files using {b}[goto]{/b}.
narrator: Each choice below jumps to a different scenario file. Open this file in the editor to see how.

> Tutorial Hub -> route_tutorial
> Branch demo -> route_branch

# ─── Route Labels ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each label below is a [goto] target. The choice menu above jumps here,
# and the [goto] command transfers execution to another scenario file.
# Add more routes by adding more labels with [goto] commands.

@label route_tutorial
[goto {{TUTORIAL_TARGET}}:start]

@label route_branch
[goto {{BRANCH_TARGET}}:start]
